<title>USA: USDA to hold meeting on E.coli testing for meat.</title>
<headline>USDA to hold meeting on E.coli testing for meat.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said it would hold a conference on Thursday next week about new methods to test meat and poultry for the presence of E. Coli bacteria.</p>
<p>The agency's Food Safety and Inspection Service said the conference will be held in suburban Washington at the Holiday Inn Rosslyn Westpark Hotel.</p>
<p>Verification testing for E. coli is required as part of the agency's Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Point Systems program.</p>
<p>((Washington commodities desk, 202 898 8467))</p>
